      "text": "The probability that a single die shows an even number is 1/2. The probability that a single die shows an odd number is also 1/2.\nWe need to find the probability that exactly 2 out of 5 dice show even numbers.\nWe can use the binomial probability formula to find this probability.\nThe binomial probability formula is P(X=k) = C(n,k) * (p^k) * (q^(n-k)), where X is the number of successes,\nn is the number of trials, k is the number of successes in each trial, p is the probability of success in each trial,\nq is the probability of failure in each trial, and C(n,k) is the number of ways to choose k successes out of n trials.\nIn this case, n=5, k=2, p=1/2, and q=1/2.\nC(5,2) = 5!/(2! * 3!) = 10.\nSo, the probability that exactly 2 out of the 5 dice show even numbers is P(X=2) = 10 * (1/2)^2 * (1/2)^3 = 10 * (1/4) * (1/8) = 10 * 1/32 = 5/16.\nTherefore, the probability is \\boxed{5/16}.",
