      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the probability that exactly two out of five 12-sided dice show an even number. Here's how we can approach this:\n\n1. **Determine the Probability of Rolling an Even Number:**\n   - A 12-sided die has numbers from 1 to 12.\n   - Half of these numbers (1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11) are even.\n\n   So, the probability \\( P(\\text{even}) \\) of rolling an even number on a single die is:\n   \\[\n   P(\\text{even}) = \\frac{6}{12} = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the Probability of Rolling an Odd Number:**\n   - The remaining numbers (2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12) are odd.\n   - Therefore, the probability \\( P(\\text{odd}) \\) of rolling an odd number on a single die is:\n   \\[\n   P(\\text{odd}) = \\frac{6}{12} = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Probability of Exactly Two Even Numbers:**\n   - We want exactly two of the five dice to show an even number.\n   - First, we need to choose 2 out of the 5 dice that will show an even number. This can be done in:\n   \\[\n   \\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{5!}{2!(5-2)!} = 10 \\text{ ways}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Each Even Number Being Rolled Exactly Once:**\n   - We know that there is 1 way to roll an even number on the chosen die.\n   - We need to roll an even number on exactly 2 of the chosen 2 dice.\n\n5. **Probability of Exactly Two Even Numbers and Two Odd Numbers:**\n   - For these 2 chosen even-numbered dice, the probability of them both showing even numbers is:\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Probability of Exactly Two Odd Numbers:**\n   - For each of the remaining \\(5-2 = 3\\) dice, the probability of them showing an odd number is:\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{1}{8}\n   \\]\n\n7. **Combine All Probabilities:**\n   - The total probability of exactly two dice showing even numbers is:\n   \\[\n   \\binom{5}{2} \\times \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 \\times \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 10 \\times \\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{8} = 10 \\times \\frac{1}{32} = \\frac{10}{32} = \\frac{5}{16}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the probability that exactly two of the dice show an even number is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{10}{32}}\\) or simplified,\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{5}{16}}.\n\\]",
